{%- set valid_phrases = [] %}
{%- for p in phrases %}
{%- if p.get("text", "").strip() %}
{%- set _ = valid_phrases.append({"text": p.get("text", "").strip(), "placement": p.get("placement", "any")}) %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% if openers %}

APPROVED OPENER — pick EXACTLY ONE. Use it as your very first line.
{% for opener in openers %}
  {{ loop.index }}. {{ opener }}
{% endfor -%}
RULE: Only ONE opener in the entire content. The other two must NOT appear.
Adapt the style to fit your angle but keep the core idea — and if the
language instruction above calls for a language other than English,
express that idea in that language; never paste this English text literally.
{% endif %}
{% if closers %}

APPROVED CLOSER — pick EXACTLY ONE. Use it as your very last line.
{% for closer in closers %}
  {{ loop.index }}. {{ closer }}
{% endfor -%}
RULE: Only ONE closer in the entire content. The other two must NOT appear anywhere.
Adapt the style to fit your angle but keep the core idea — and if the
language instruction above calls for a language other than English,
express that idea in that language; never paste this English text literally.
{% endif %}
{% if valid_phrases %}

REQUIRED PHRASES — weave the MEANING of each of these naturally into the
content. These are written in English here only to tell you what idea to
include. If the language instruction above calls for a language other than
English, express each phrase's meaning in that language, in your own
words — never insert the English text itself, not even in quotes:
{% for phrase in valid_phrases %}
  - '{{ phrase.text }}' (placement: {{ phrase.placement }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
